# Do these names tell the truth?
subtitle: "Three famous names, three fibs: guess how long the Hundred Years' War lasted, where Panama hats are made and where guinea pigs come from."

## Do these names tell the truth?
feedback:
    style: warm
    perfect: Nobody's name fools you.
    good: You saw through most of them.
    poor: These names have fooled people for centuries.
    none: The names won this round.
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: hyw
      title: Hundred Years' War
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2025
      finding: intermittent conflict between England and France, 1337-1453
    - id: hat
      title: Traditional weaving of the Ecuadorian toquilla straw hat
      authors: UNESCO
      year: 2012
      finding: the so-called Panama hat is woven in Ecuador from toquilla palm fibre; inscribed on the Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2012
    - id: cavy
      title: Guinea pig
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2025
      finding: a South American rodent, domesticated in the Andes thousands of years ago; still raised for food there

    icon war size 320 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of "crossed swords" hidden true
    text war_l "Hundred Years' War" x 500 y 225 font_size 50 hidden true
    text war_v "116 years" #b5482e x 830 y 450 font_size 56 hidden true
    icon hat size 320 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of "womans hat" hidden true
    text hat_l "Panama hat" x 500 y 225 font_size 50 hidden true
    text hat_v "Ecuador" #b5482e x 830 y 450 font_size 56 hidden true
    icon pig size 320 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of hamster hidden true
    text pig_l "Guinea pig" x 500 y 225 font_size 50 hidden true
    text pig_v "The Andes" #b5482e x 830 y 450 font_size 56 hidden true

    card title "Do these names tell the truth?"

A: Three famous names, and every one of them tells a fib. Can you spot where?
    icon r1 size 220 set twemoji x 200 y 430 icon_look picture of "crossed swords"
    icon r2 size 220 set twemoji x 500 y 430 icon_look picture of "womans hat"
    icon r3 size 220 set twemoji x 800 y 430 icon_look picture of hamster
    parallel true

    hide r1 r2 r3

A: First, the Hundred Years' War, between England and France.
    draw war war_l

    quiz "How long did the Hundred Years' War last?"
        right: A hundred and sixteen years: England and France fought on and off from 1337 to 1453.
        * 99 years
        * 100 years
        + 116 years

    draw war_v

    pause 1.5

B: A hundred and sixteen? I'd have said a hundred, obviously.
    highlight war_v

    hide war war_l war_v

B: Next one. The Panama hat. Surely that one's safe?
    draw hat hat_l

    quiz "Where are Panama hats made?"
        right: Ecuador. They are woven from toquilla palm straw, around towns like Montecristi and Cuenca.
        * Panama
        + Ecuador
        * Cuba

    draw hat_v

    pause 1.5

A: They were shipped out through Panama, and the workers who dug the canal wore them.
    highlight hat_l

    hide hat hat_l hat_v

B: And the guinea pig. At least that's from Guinea?
    draw pig pig_l

    quiz "Where do guinea pigs come from?"
        right: The Andes of South America, where people tamed them thousands of years ago, and still eat them today.
        * Guinea, in Africa
        + The Andes
        * New Guinea

    draw pig_v

    pause 1.5

B: So not from Guinea. And not a pig either.
    highlight pig_l

    hide pig pig_l pig_v

A: You got {score} of {score_total}. Three names, three fibs.
    draw r1 r2 r3 parallel true

A: As for the guinea pig: it's a rodent. It just squeals a bit like a piglet.
    highlight r3

